  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1234 AM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nWarmer conditions return over the weekend with ridging aloft \ntransitioning to southwest flow ahead of a filling upper low \nentering southern CA and western AZ on Sunday.  Saturday remains dry \nacross southern CO but some moisture advects in for Sunday and \nMonday as this weakening upper level disturbance gradually lifts out \nacross CO.  Some isolated showers will be possible, mainly for the \nmountain areas with some spotty light rainfall possible.  Snow \nlevels will remain above 10000 feet during the day time hours when \nshowers will be most prevalent. \n\nThe next upper trough moves into the west coast Tuesday and \nWednesday.  This will increase southwest flow over CO bringing \nbreezy and warm conditions with increasing showers across the \nContinental Divide.  Best chances for showers will be across the \neastern San Juans due to orographically favored southwest flow, \nhowever this will be warm system with snow levels remaining high.  \n\nUpper low will translate through the western U.S. towards CO into \nlate week, though details on timing, track and strength are highly \nvariable at this point.  Trend will be towards unsettled weather and \na cool down perhaps next weekend as the system crosses the Rockies.\n-KT",
